# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the two values from Supabase
# (Project Settings -> API). `.env.local` is git-ignored, so it stays on your Mac.
#
# Both values are *meant* to be public — they get compiled into the JavaScript
# every visitor downloads. That is how Supabase is designed. The anon key on its
# own can do exactly two things, because the database rules say so:
#   1. read recommendations you have listed
#   2. submit a new one, which always arrives as "pending"
# It cannot publish, edit, delete, or read anybody's email address.
#
# The same two values also need to be set as repository secrets on GitHub, or
# the deployed site won't be able to load anything. See HOW-TO-EDIT.md 7b.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste-the-anon-public-key-here
